7. License Workflows
LW.1 New License
User story: As a License Administrator, I want to create a license for a new customer deployment so that the customer can receive the appropriate license artifact.

Workflow

Select Customer
      ↓
Select Environment
      ↓
Select Product
      ↓
Select Version
      ↓
Select License Type
      ↓
Enter Entitlement
      ↓
Enter License Term
      ↓
Submit Request
      ↓
Validation
      ↓
Approval
      ↓
License Generation
      ↓
License Issued

Requirements

FR-LIC-001: The system shall allow an authorized user to initiate a new license request.

FR-LIC-002: The request shall identify the customer.

FR-LIC-003: The request shall identify the customer environment.

FR-LIC-004: The request shall identify the product and version.

FR-LIC-005: The request shall specify the license type.

FR-LIC-006 The request shall specify license entitlement.

FR-LIC-007: The request shall specify start and expiration dates.

FR-LIC-008: The system shall validate required fields.

FR-LIC-009: The system shall route the request through configured approval rules.

FR-LIC-010: After approval, the system shall generate the license.

 

LW.2 License Generation Formats
The system shall generate a license artifact based on approved license information.

·       Possible formats include JSON / XML /

·       Signed token / Product-specific license file

The format should be configurable per product.

LW.3 License generation requirements

·       FR-GEN-001: Every generated license shall have a unique license identifier.

·       FR-GEN-002: The generated license shall contain the required entitlement and validity information.

·       FR-GEN-003: The generated license should be digitally signed when required by the organization’s licensing model.

·       FR-GEN-004: Private signing keys shall not be stored in the application database.

·       FR-GEN-005: License generation shall be auditable.

Important boundary

·       The license artifact is generated by LLMS, but LLMS does not send or install the license into the customer’s product deployment.

LW.4 License Renewal

A user shall be able to request renewal of an existing license.

The previous license must remain available in history.

Example:

Existing

 

License 1001
Jan 1, 2026 → Dec 31, 2026

Renewal

 

License 1057
Jan 1, 2027 → Dec 31, 2027

 

 

LW.4 License Upgrade

An upgrade changes the recorded product version associated with the deployment/license.

Example:

From:

Deployment
Product A
Version 5.1
License L1001

Upgrade To

Deployment
Product A
Version 5.2
License L1050

 

Requirements: The system shall:

·       Identify the current deployment.

·       Display the current version.

·       Display allowed target versions.

·       Validate configured transition rules.

·       Create an upgrade request.

·       Obtain required approval.

·       Generate a new license.

·       Update the deployment record.

·       Preserve the previous license.

·       Create a lifecycle event.

Important:

·       The system does not verify whether the customer upgraded the software.

·       The recorded deployment version changes based on an authorized business transaction/update.

LW.5 License Downgrade
The downgrade workflow shall operate similarly.

The system shall:

·       Identify current version

·       Identify allowed target versions

·       Validate business rules

·       Obtain approval where required

·       Generate the new license

·       Update the deployment record

·       Preserve previous license

·       Record lifecycle event

LW.6. License Replacement
Replacement shall be supported when:

·       License was generated incorrectly

·       License artifact was lost

·       License needs to be regenerated

·       Security incident requires replacement

·       Other approved business reasons

The old license must remain in history.

LW.7 License Revocation
Authorized users shall be able to revoke licenses.

Required:

·       Reason

·       Requestor

·       Approver where required

·       Timestamp

Status become: Revoked

The system does not deactivate the actual deployed product.

LW.8 Expiration Management
The system shall automatically calculate:

Days Until Expiration

Example:

Expiration Date: December 31, 2026
Current Date: September 16, 2026

Days Remaining: 106

The application shall classify licenses as:

·       Active

·       Expiring Soon

·       Expired

Thresholds shall be configurable.

